# Database Restructure Plan — Base + Extension Tables

> **Status:** Planning (not yet approved for implementation)  
> **Target Phase:** 5 or 6 (after current feature work is stable)  
> **Risk Level:** High — touches every layer of the stack  

---

## Problem Statement

The current schema has user data scattered across **4 tables** (`auth.users`, `profiles`, `students`, `instructors`) with duplicated columns (`email`, `name`, `branch`, `department`), no formal relationships between them, and a painful "linking" problem where seed scripts must stitch auth accounts to profile rows to domain rows manually.

## Design Philosophy

**One base table for identity. Extension tables for role-specific data.**

Every person in the system — admin, teacher, or student — is first and foremost a **user**. What differs between them is the *extra data* their role requires. A student has a semester and SBRN. A teacher has a faculty code and designation. An admin has permission scopes. The base table captures what's universal; extension tables capture what's role-specific.

---

## Proposed Schema

### Entity Relationship Diagram

```mermaid
erDiagram
    AUTH_USERS ||--|| USERS : "1:1 (id = auth.uid)"
    USERS ||--o| STUDENT_DETAILS : "if role = student"
    USERS ||--o| TEACHER_DETAILS : "if role = teacher"
    USERS ||--o| ADMIN_DETAILS : "if role = admin"
    USERS ||--o{ FACE_EMBEDDINGS : "has"
    USERS ||--o{ ACTIVITY_LOGS : "generates"
    USERS ||--o{ ENROLLMENTS : "participates in"
    COURSES ||--o{ ENROLLMENTS : "has"
    USERS ||--o{ ATTENDANCE : "marked in"
    COURSES ||--o{ ATTENDANCE : "tracked by"
    COURSES ||--o{ TIMETABLE_ENTRIES : "scheduled as"
```

---

### Table Definitions

#### 1. `users` (base table — replaces `profiles` + `students` + `instructors`)

This is the **single source of truth** for every person in the system. It maps 1:1 to `auth.users` via the UUID primary key.

| Column | Type | Constraints | Notes |
|--------|------|-------------|-------|
| `id` | `UUID` | PK, FK → `auth.users(id)` ON DELETE CASCADE | Supabase Auth UUID |
| `role` | `user_role` ENUM | NOT NULL, `('admin','teacher','student')` | Authoritative role |
| `email` | `TEXT` | NOT NULL, UNIQUE | Login email |
| `full_name` | `TEXT` | NOT NULL | Display name |
| `phone` | `TEXT` | | Optional contact |
| `avatar_url` | `TEXT` | | Profile photo URL (Supabase Storage) |
| `branch` | `TEXT` | | Engineering branch |
| `approval_status` | `TEXT` | NOT NULL DEFAULT `'approved'`, CHECK `('pending','approved','rejected')` | Gates login |
| `is_active` | `BOOLEAN` | NOT NULL DEFAULT `true` | Soft-delete flag |
| `created_at` | `TIMESTAMPTZ` | NOT NULL DEFAULT `NOW()` | |
| `updated_at` | `TIMESTAMPTZ` | NOT NULL DEFAULT `NOW()` | Auto-updated via trigger |

**Key decisions:**
- `branch` is on the base table because teachers also belong to a branch/department
- `role` remains an ENUM for type safety and fast filtering
- `approval_status` replaces the old two-place check (profiles + students.status)
- No more duplicate `name`/`email` across tables

---

#### 2. `student_details` (extension for students only)

| Column | Type | Constraints | Notes |
|--------|------|-------------|-------|
| `user_id` | `UUID` | PK, FK → `users(id)` ON DELETE CASCADE | 1:1 with users |
| `sbrn` | `TEXT` | NOT NULL, UNIQUE | Student Board Roll Number (e.g. `2024CE001`) |
| `semester` | `INTEGER` | NOT NULL, CHECK `(1-6)` | Current semester |
| `session` | `TEXT` | NOT NULL | Academic session (e.g. `2024 - 2027`) |
| `section` | `TEXT` | | Section/division if applicable |
| `registration_date` | `DATE` | DEFAULT `CURRENT_DATE` | When student registered |
| `attendance_rate` | `NUMERIC(5,2)` | DEFAULT `0.00` | Cached overall % |

**Why separate?** An admin or teacher row should never have `sbrn` or `semester` columns. This keeps the schema honest — if a row exists in `student_details`, that user IS a student, enforced by structure, not just a column value.

---

#### 3. `teacher_details` (extension for teachers only)

| Column | Type | Constraints | Notes |
|--------|------|-------------|-------|
| `user_id` | `UUID` | PK, FK → `users(id)` ON DELETE CASCADE | 1:1 with users |
| `faculty_code` | `TEXT` | UNIQUE | e.g. `FAC-CS-001` |
| `designation` | `TEXT` | | Professor / Asst. Professor / HOD |
| `specialization` | `TEXT` | | Area of expertise |
| `joining_date` | `DATE` | | |

---

#### 4. `admin_details` (extension for admins only)

| Column | Type | Constraints | Notes |
|--------|------|-------------|-------|
| `user_id` | `UUID` | PK, FK → `users(id)` ON DELETE CASCADE | 1:1 with users |
| `permission_scope` | `TEXT` | DEFAULT `'full'` | `'full'`, `'readonly'`, `'department'` |
| `managed_branches` | `TEXT[]` | | Which branches this admin manages (for department-scoped admins) |

> [!NOTE]
> `admin_details` is thin right now. It exists for forward-compatibility — when you add multi-admin support with scoped permissions, the table is ready.

---

#### 5. `face_embeddings` (replaces filesystem `.npy`/`.pkl`)

| Column | Type | Constraints | Notes |
|--------|------|-------------|-------|
| `id` | `BIGINT` | PK, GENERATED | Auto-increment |
| `user_id` | `UUID` | FK → `users(id)`, NOT NULL | Who this face belongs to |
| `embedding` | `FLOAT8[]` | NOT NULL | 128-dim feature vector from face model |
| `sample_count` | `INTEGER` | DEFAULT `0` | How many frames were used |
| `model_version` | `TEXT` | DEFAULT `'haar_knn_v1'` | Which model generated this |
| `enrolled_at` | `TIMESTAMPTZ` | DEFAULT `NOW()` | |
| `is_active` | `BOOLEAN` | DEFAULT `true` | Can soft-delete old enrollments |

**Runtime usage:** The Python face engine loads all active embeddings into a numpy array on startup, exactly like today. The DB is the durable store; memory is the runtime cache. On enrollment, write to DB → reload cache.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The face engine currently uses `.npy` + `.pkl` files. Migration requires a one-time script to extract existing embeddings and INSERT them into this table, then update `server.py` to read from DB on startup.

---

#### 6. `courses` (mostly unchanged)

| Column | Type | Constraints | Notes |
|--------|------|-------------|-------|
| `id` | `BIGINT` | PK, GENERATED | |
| `course_code` | `TEXT` | NOT NULL, UNIQUE | e.g. `CS-301` |
| `course_name` | `TEXT` | NOT NULL | |
| `branch` | `TEXT` | NOT NULL | Which branch offers this |
| `semester` | `INTEGER` | NOT NULL | Which semester |
| `credits` | `INTEGER` | | |
| `status` | `TEXT` | DEFAULT `'active'` | |
| `created_at` | `TIMESTAMPTZ` | DEFAULT `NOW()` | |

---

#### 7. `enrollments` (replaces `course_instructors` + implicit student-course link)

| Column | Type | Constraints | Notes |
|--------|------|-------------|-------|
| `id` | `BIGINT` | PK, GENERATED | |
| `user_id` | `UUID` | FK → `users(id)`, NOT NULL | Student OR teacher |
| `course_id` | `BIGINT` | FK → `courses(id)`, NOT NULL | |
| `role_in_course` | `TEXT` | NOT NULL, CHECK `('student','instructor')` | Distinguishes students from teachers in the same table |
| `enrolled_at` | `TIMESTAMPTZ` | DEFAULT `NOW()` | |
| UNIQUE | | `(user_id, course_id)` | One enrollment per user per course |

**Why this is better:** Currently there's no explicit student↔course relationship — attendance records implicitly create it. With `enrollments`, you can:
- Show "My Courses" for both students and teachers
- Know class size before any attendance is taken
- Remove a student from a course without deleting their attendance history

---

#### 8. `attendance` (streamlined)

| Column | Type | Constraints | Notes |
|--------|------|-------------|-------|
| `id` | `BIGINT` | PK, GENERATED | |
| `user_id` | `UUID` | FK → `users(id)`, NOT NULL | The student |
| `course_id` | `BIGINT` | FK → `courses(id)`, NOT NULL | |
| `date_attended` | `DATE` | NOT NULL, DEFAULT `CURRENT_DATE` | |
| `status` | `TEXT` | NOT NULL, DEFAULT `'absent'`, CHECK `('present','absent','late')` | |
| `marked_by` | `UUID` | FK → `users(id)` | Teacher or face engine user who marked it |
| `source` | `TEXT` | DEFAULT `'manual'`, CHECK `('face_recognition','manual','bulk_import')` | How was this record created |
| `confidence` | `NUMERIC(5,2)` | | Face recognition confidence % (NULL if manual) |
| `marked_at` | `TIMESTAMPTZ` | DEFAULT `NOW()` | Exact time of marking |
| UNIQUE | | `(user_id, course_id, date_attended)` | Prevent duplicates |

**New columns explained:**
- `marked_by` — accountability. Was it auto-marked by the face engine or manually by a teacher?
- `source` — distinguishes face-scanned vs manual vs bulk-imported attendance
- `confidence` — the face recognition confidence score, useful for audit

---

#### 9. `timetable_entries` (mostly unchanged)

| Column | Type | Constraints | Notes |
|--------|------|-------------|-------|
| `id` | `BIGINT` | PK, GENERATED | |
| `course_id` | `BIGINT` | FK → `courses(id)` | Links to course |
| `branch` | `TEXT` | NOT NULL | |
| `semester` | `INTEGER` | NOT NULL | |
| `day_of_week` | `TEXT` | NOT NULL, CHECK days | |
| `start_time` | `TIME` | NOT NULL | |
| `end_time` | `TIME` | NOT NULL | |
| `room` | `TEXT` | | Room/Lab |
| `teacher_id` | `UUID` | FK → `users(id)` | Who teaches this slot |
| `batch_group` | `TEXT` | | For lab batches |

---

#### 10. `activity_logs` (new)

| Column | Type | Constraints | Notes |
|--------|------|-------------|-------|
| `id` | `BIGINT` | PK, GENERATED | |
| `user_id` | `UUID` | FK → `users(id)` | Who performed the action |
| `action` | `TEXT` | NOT NULL | e.g. `'login'`, `'mark_attendance'`, `'approve_student'`, `'enroll_face'` |
| `entity_type` | `TEXT` | | What was acted on: `'student'`, `'course'`, `'attendance'` |
| `entity_id` | `TEXT` | | ID of the entity |
| `details` | `JSONB` | | Arbitrary metadata |
| `ip_address` | `TEXT` | | |
| `created_at` | `TIMESTAMPTZ` | DEFAULT `NOW()` | |

**Index:** `CREATE INDEX idx_logs_user_time ON activity_logs(user_id, created_at DESC);`

